## Application-Owned Tables

All tables owned by this application must use the prefix:

yorapet_*

Current application-owned tables:

- `yorapet_users` — authenticated application users
- `yorapet_company_profiles` — company profile settings
- `yorapet_purchase` — purchase lines synced from `tallydata_purchases` (matched by `sync_key` content hash; includes `box` / `qty_per_box` from Tally; calculated `value_addition` / `cost_value` / `cost_price` for FIFO)
- `yorapet_purchase_expense` — voucher-level `expenses` + `credit_note` total (keyed by voucher_no + voucher_date)
- `yorapet_purchase_line_credit` — manual per-line credit notes keyed by purchase `sync_key` (survives Tally sync)
- `yorapet_purchase_credit_note` — legacy stock-item credit notes (superseded by costing-page line credits)
- `yorapet_sales` — sales lines synced from `tallydata_sales` (matched by `sync_key` content hash)
- `yorapet_opening_stock` — opening stock balances for FIFO costing
- `yorapet_inventory_extra` — app-owned stock item fields (weight, neck size, qty per box, box dimension, reorder level) keyed by `stock_item` from `tallydata_inventorymaster`
- `yorapet_inventory_image` — up to 4 images per stock item (BLOB + content type), keyed by `stock_item`

Rules

- Every new application-owned table must be named `yorapet_<purpose>`.
- SQLAlchemy models using `Base` must set `__tablename__` with the `yorapet_` prefix.
- Never create application-owned tables without the `yorapet_` prefix.
- Never rename `yorapet_*` tables to unprefixed names.
- Include all `yorapet_*` tables in Alembic migrations.
- Application features requiring additional data must use separate `yorapet_*` tables that reference legacy tables when appropriate.

